{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836058",
      "title": "Creating Reusable Components & Component Combinations",
      "sourceHash": "64aef90b0cd41066fc124913138c1ef164dcd8c6d89c47c4a039035048e8afa9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "Now before we'll move on to Tailwind CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "the last and pretty popular approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "for styling React components and applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 11.55,
          "en": "I wanna show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.55,
          "end": 12.75,
          "en": "I wanna take another look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.75,
          "end": 16.02,
          "en": "at these styled components we created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "For example, here in the AuthInputs.jsx file, you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "that quite a lot of new components were added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 28.233,
          "en": "This div, this label, this input, and this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 31.95,
          "en": "Now there are some components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.95,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "most importantly that div here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 39.2,
          "en": "which really only are used in AuthInputs.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.24,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "Here I'm using this ControlContainer component down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "and it's unlikely that I need that same component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "in other parts of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 53.28,
          "en": "And in such cases, storing it here in that same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 55.863,
          "en": "is perfect and is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "But for the label and the input and the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "it's not unlikely that in a bigger application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 69.337,
          "en": "I might need those same components with the same styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.337,
          "end": 72.423,
          "en": "in other parts of the application as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "And therefore you could consider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "creating separate component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "for such kinds of components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "So UI elements that you may reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.40299999999999,
          "en": "in other parts of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "And therefore we could add a Button.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 94.95,
          "en": "and an Input.jsx file and maybe also a Label.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.95,
          "end": 98.013,
          "en": "to store those styled components in those files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "Though, at least when it comes to the input and the label,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "I'll show you yet another approach or pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "you might want to consider for your applications as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 111.003,
          "en": "but let's start with the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 117.2,
          "en": "We can simply grab this button here, cut it from AuthInputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 121.953,
          "en": "and paste it into the Button.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.94,
          "end": 126.33,
          "en": "And then here we can simply export this constant button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.33,
          "end": 127.893,
          "en": "as a default like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "And of course, since I'm using styled in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "I now also have to import styled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.953,
          "en": "from styled-components like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "And with that exported and set up like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "we can go back to AuthInputs.jsx, and there of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 151.07,
          "en": "simply import the button from our Button.jsx file like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "And therefore AuthInputs.jsx will still work as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 159.69,
          "en": "the button will still work as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.69,
          "end": 162.663,
          "en": "but we could now use it in other files as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "Which of course does not matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "for this super simple dummy application here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "but which will likely matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 173.493,
          "en": "in bigger React applications you might be building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "Now when it comes to the label and the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 183.11,
          "en": "we could do the same, but here I'd argue that it's so common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "to this combination of label and input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 189.96,
          "en": "that we might wanna merge them to gather",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.96,
          "end": 192.213,
          "en": "into one single component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.44,
          "end": 198.44,
          "en": "And for that we could grab this input and label components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 203.85,
          "en": "so these two styled components in the AuthInputs.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 208.563,
          "en": "and cut them and move them here into Input.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 209.85,
          "end": 213.45,
          "en": "Then we of course also need to import styled here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 213.45,
          "end": 218.45,
          "en": "from styled-components, but now I will actually not export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 222.24,
          "en": "these two components like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 222.24,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "but instead I'll export a new component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 229.143,
          "en": "which I'll name CustomInput to avoid a name clash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 236.06,
          "en": "where I will simply return a paragraph as a wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 241.413,
          "en": "where I then use my styled label and my styled input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 247.02,
          "en": "But now here on this custom input component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 247.02,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "which is a regular component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 253.26,
          "en": "as we built it many times before in this course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 256.17,
          "en": "I'll accept a label prop, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 256.17,
          "end": 257.55,
          "en": "and since it's my component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 257.55,
          "end": 259.863,
          "en": "I can accept any prop I want here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 260.76,
          "end": 263.55,
          "en": "and I'll then merge any other props I'll get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.55,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "into a props object with this three dot operator here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 271.383,
          "en": "which can be used when using object destructuring like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "This allows me to pass this label text as a child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 280.383,
          "en": "between these style component label tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 284.82,
          "en": "And here on the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 284.82,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "I'll spread my remaining props which I'm getting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "so that for example, the onChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 295.053,
          "en": "gets forwarded to that input, or the type prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 296.31,
          "end": 299.37,
          "en": "In addition, I'll expect an invalid prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 299.37,
          "end": 302.31,
          "en": "on my custom input, and I'll use it as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 302.31,
          "end": 304.83,
          "en": "for the dollar sign invalid prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 304.83,
          "end": 307.413,
          "en": "which is expected by my styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 308.94,
          "end": 311.853,
          "en": "And I'll use that for both the label and the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 314.16,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "And with that I got custom input component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 318.69,
          "en": "which is exported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 318.69,
          "end": 322.08299999999997,
          "en": "and we can now use that in AuthInputs.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 323.4,
          "end": 328.4,
          "en": "In there I can now import my custom input from Input.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 331.32,
          "end": 334.59000000000003,
          "en": "and here in this file I can just name it Input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 334.59000000000003,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "The name here can differ",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 338.8,
          "en": "from my component function file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 339.84000000000003,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "Because it is the default export,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 346.203,
          "en": "and therefore imported like this here in AuthInputs.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 348,
          "end": 350.31,
          "en": "And now I can use this custom input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 350.31,
          "end": 353.1,
          "en": "instead of separately setting up the label,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 353.1,
          "end": 358.1,
          "en": "or this paragraph here, I can get rid of all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 362.28,
          "end": 365.04,
          "en": "And instead, now here I have my input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 365.04,
          "end": 368.05,
          "en": "which now receives just a prop named invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 369.84,
          "end": 372.72,
          "en": "and a label prop, which here is Email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 372.72,
          "end": 375.39,
          "en": "And then these props, which will be forwarded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 375.39,
          "end": 379.323,
          "en": "to the underlying input due to how this is set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 382.38,
          "end": 385.68,
          "en": "And the second input here also gets the invalid prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 385.68,
          "end": 388.923,
          "en": "therefore, and also a label of Password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 391.59,
          "end": 395.67,
          "en": "With that if I saved it and reload these inputs and labels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 395.67,
          "end": 400.17,
          "en": "still work as before, I can still enter values in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 400.17,
          "end": 403.56,
          "en": "and submit valid values therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 403.56,
          "end": 408.56,
          "en": "but now I got this reusable combined input component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 409.02,
          "end": 412.44,
          "en": "and you could absolutely use this pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 412.44,
          "end": 414.09000000000003,
          "en": "this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 414.09000000000003,
          "end": 417.33,
          "en": "also, if you were not using styled components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 417.33,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "because of course you could have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 421.44,
          "en": "just simply added regular CSS classes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 421.44,
          "end": 426.44,
          "en": "or target the label and input with regular CSS classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 427.29,
          "end": 429.69,
          "en": "The main takeaway from this lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 429.69,
          "end": 433.89,
          "en": "therefore simply is that as a React developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 433.89,
          "end": 437.64,
          "en": "you should always look for opportunities like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 437.64,
          "end": 441.96,
          "en": "where you can either outsource reusable components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 441.96,
          "end": 444.84,
          "en": "that have a certain styling applied to them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 444.84,
          "end": 447.963,
          "en": "which you might need in different parts of the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 449.1,
          "end": 454.1,
          "en": "and/or components that maybe have certain combinations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 454.5,
          "end": 457.92,
          "en": "of JSX elements that you might need to reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 457.92,
          "end": 460.44,
          "en": "in other parts of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 460.44,
          "end": 464.61,
          "en": "And in the end, this is something we already have been doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 464.61,
          "end": 467.82,
          "en": "in all these other sections up to this point already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 467.82,
          "end": 470.67,
          "en": "But now we're also taking styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 470.67,
          "end": 473.31,
          "en": "as another factor into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 473.31,
          "end": 475.77,
          "en": "that might influence our choices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 475.77,
          "end": 478.89,
          "en": "regarding how we split our components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 478.89,
          "end": 481.833,
          "en": "and how we reuse our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 482.82,
          "end": 485.88,
          "en": "And that's it for styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 485.88,
          "end": 488.07,
          "en": "Styled components have the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 488.07,
          "end": 492.09,
          "en": "of being relatively quick and easy to set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 492.09,
          "end": 494.76,
